  "counts": "Approximate, not a hard cap. PNAS sets length in journal pages, not words: 'A standard 6-page article is approximately 4,000 words, 50 references, and 4 medium-size graphical elements (i.e., figures and tables).' 'The preferred length of Direct Submission articles remains at 6 pages, but PNAS will allow articles up to a maximum of 12 pages.' The template doesn't say which parts the 4,000 words cover, and it gives no word count for 12 pages. main_text_words, references and display_items here are those 6-page equivalents.",
  "notes": "pnas.org (Author Center) returned HTTP 403 to automated reading. These values come from PNAS's own LaTeX template on Overleaf: author National Academy of Sciences, tagged 'PNAS - Official Templates', 2025 edition. summary_words is the Significance Statement: 'between 50 and 120 words in length', written for scientists outside the field, and required for Research Reports. Abstract: 'no more than 250 words in a single paragraph'. Keywords: 'At least three keywords are required at submission. Please provide three to five keywords, separated by the pipe symbol.' Suggested section order: introduction (no heading), results, discussion, materials and methods, acknowledgments, references. Detailed methods may go in the SI Appendix, but the main text must still carry sufficient methods. The template's footnote section says 'The article should contain only 13 footnotes'; this may be example text. Brief Reports (for comparison): 3 pages, about 1,600 words (including the manuscript text, title page, abstract and figure legends), 15 references, no significance statement, and no supporting text, tables or figures. 2026-11-16: the Internet Archive's copy (2026-06-17) of https://www.pnas.org/author-center/submitting-your-manuscript was read: title '< 135 characters'; abstract 'no more than 250 words'; Significance statement 'Include no more than 120 words' (the template's 50-word minimum stands; the page gives none); 'Include at least three keywords at submission.' 2026-11-16: pnas.org's Submitting your manuscript page read in a browser: Research Reports preferably six pages, at most 12; 'a standard six-page article is approximately 4,000 words, 50 references, and four medium-size graphical elements'; abstract no more than 250 words; significance statement no more than 120 words; title under 135 characters; at least three keywords.",
